hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1488","Imran bin Musa Al-Qazzaz brought us strange news, Abdul-Warith brought us, Abdul-Aziz, who is Ibn Suhayb, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not come out to us three times, so prayer was performed, so Abu Bakr went to lead the people in prayer, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose He raised the veil, and we did not see a sight more astonishing to us than it, where the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appeared clearly to us. Then the Messenger of God nodded. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he told Abu Bakr to come forward, and the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, loosened the veil, and we did not reach it until he died, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “Peace be upon him.” Abu Bakr said: This piece of news is of the type that I knew, that the understandable signal from the speaker may take the place of logic, since the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Al-Siddiq understood by referring to him that he had commanded him to lead the Imamate, so he contented himself with referring to him when pronouncing his command to reside."
